2. What Data We Collect and Process
To provide the core functions of the bot (in particular, automated TikTok live notifications), we process exclusively the technically necessary data.

a) Automatically Processed Discord Data
When the bot is installed on a Discord server or when commands are executed, we store/process:

Server IDs (Guild IDs): For the unique assignment of server settings.

Channel IDs: To know in which text channel the TikTok notifications should be posted.

Role IDs (Optional): If you configure a specific role to be pinged when a live stream starts (e.g., @everyone or a custom live role).

b) Processed TikTok Data
TikTok Usernames / Handles: The TikTok profile names you register in the bot whose live status is to be monitored.

Publicly Accessible Live Status Data: Information on whether the respective profile is currently live, as well as publicly available stream details (e.g., stream title, thumbnail URL, stream link) to generate the notification card on Discord.

3. Purpose and Legal Basis of Data Processing
Data processing is carried out for the following purposes:

Providing and executing the functions of the bot (e.g., triggering Discord notifications when a TikTok live stream starts).

Storing server configurations so that settings are retained after a restart of the bot.

Legal Basis: Processing is based on Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR (performance of a contract or provision of the service requested by the user) as well as Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR (our legitimate interest in the secure and functional provision of the bot).

4. Retention Period
Configuration Data (Server & Channel IDs, Linked TikTok Names): Stored as long as the bot is present on your server and the integration is active.

Deletion Upon Bot Removal: If the bot is removed from a server (kicked/banned) or if a notification is deleted via a bot command, the associated configuration data will be removed from our database within a reasonable timeframe.

5. Sharing Data with Third Parties
We never sell, rent, or trade your data.

Discord API: To create messages and interact with the Discord client, data is transmitted via the official Discord API.

TikTok Data / API: To query the live status, the stored public TikTok profile names are matched with publicly accessible interfaces.

6. Your Rights (Data Subject Rights)
Under the GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your stored data:

Right of Access (Art. 15 GDPR): You can request information about what data is stored regarding your server or account.

Right to Rectification & Erasure (Art. 16 & 17 GDPR): You can request the correction or complete deletion of your configuration data.

Right to Object (Art. 21 GDPR): You can object to the further processing of your data at any time.

To exercise your rights, simply contact the address specified in Section 1.

7. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We reserve the right to update or modify this Privacy Policy as needed (e.g., due to new bot features or legal changes). The date of the last update at the top of this page will be adjusted accordingly.

